    <string name="lesson_b1_title">Posture and holding the violin</string>
    <string name="lesson_b1_goal">Hold the violin without tension so you can play for a long time without getting tired.</string>
    <string name="lesson_b1_steps">Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart · Rest the violin on your left collarbone and your jaw on the chin rest · Hold it for one minute without the left hand, only with the weight of your head · Relax your shoulders and neck and repeat three times</string>
    <string name="lesson_b2_title">Holding the bow</string>
    <string name="lesson_b2_goal">Hold the bow with a relaxed hand and rounded fingers.</string>
    <string name="lesson_b2_steps">Practise first with a pencil: bent thumb opposite the middle finger · Move to the bow: thumb between the frog and the stick, little finger curved on top of the stick · Hold the bow in the air for ten seconds without squeezing · Make small finger movements up and down</string>
    <string name="lesson_b3_title">Open strings</string>
    <string name="lesson_b3_goal">Make a clean sound with a straight bow, parallel to the bridge.</string>
    <string name="lesson_b3_steps">Set the metronome to 60 · Play each string (G, D, A, E) four beats down-bow and four beats up-bow · Keep the bow between the bridge and the fingerboard · Listen for a broken sound and adjust the weight of your arm</string>
    <string name="lesson_b4_title">Tuning the violin</string>
    <string name="lesson_b4_goal">Tune the four strings on your own with the app tuner.</string>
    <string name="lesson_b4_steps">Start with A (440 Hz) · Use the fine tuners for small adjustments · Then tune D, G and E · Play two strings together to check the fifth</string>
    <string name="lesson_e1_title">First finger pattern</string>
    <string name="lesson_e1_goal">Place fingers 1, 2 and 3 with 2 and 3 together and in tune.</string>
    <string name="lesson_e1_steps">On the A string play A, B, C sharp and D · Check each note with the tuner · Repeat on the D string (D, E, F sharp, G) · Keep the fingers down as you go up</string>
    <string name="lesson_e2_title">D major scale</string>
    <string name="lesson_e2_goal">Play the one-octave D major scale in tune and in time.</string>
    <string name="lesson_e2_steps">Metronome at 60, one note per beat · Play the scale up and down three times · Move to two notes per beat when it sounds clean · Take care when crossing from the D string to the A string</string>
    <string name="lesson_e3_title">Bow distribution</string>
    <string name="lesson_e3_goal">Share out the bow so the sound stays even from start to end.</string>
    <string name="lesson_e3_steps">Metronome at 60 · Whole bow in four beats, then in two · Half bow (upper and lower half) in one beat · Listen that the sound does not fade at the end of the bow</string>
    <string name="lesson_e4_title">String crossings</string>
    <string name="lesson_e4_goal">Move between strings without noise, using the arm rather than the wrist.</string>
    <string name="lesson_e4_steps">Metronome at 72 · Alternate open A and E, two notes per beat · Bring the elbow to the level of the next string in advance · Repeat with D and A, then with G and D</string>
    <string name="lesson_i1_title">Two-octave G major scale</string>
    <string name="lesson_i1_goal">Cover the violin from the G string to the E string with good intonation.</string>
    <string name="lesson_i1_steps">Metronome at 72, one note per beat · Play the scale up and down · Move to two and then four notes per beat · Note the pitches that drift and repeat them slowly</string>
    <string name="lesson_i2_title">Dynamics and contact point</string>
    <string name="lesson_i2_goal">Control volume with bow weight, speed and contact point.</string>
    <string name="lesson_i2_steps">Play a long note piano near the fingerboard · Repeat forte moving towards the bridge · Make a crescendo and a diminuendo in a single bow · Practise on every string</string>
    <string name="lesson_i3_title">Third position</string>
    <string name="lesson_i3_goal">Shift the hand to third position and back without losing intonation.</string>
    <string name="lesson_i3_steps">On the A string play D with the first finger in third position · Check with the tuner before going on · Practise the shift from first to third with the same finger, sliding gently · Play the D major scale starting in third position</string>
    <string name="lesson_i4_title">Preparing vibrato</string>
    <string name="lesson_i4_goal">Prepare the vibrato motion slowly and evenly.</string>
    <string name="lesson_i4_steps">Without the bow, rest the second finger on the A string · Move the hand towards the bridge and back, two motions per beat at 60 · Go up to three and four motions per beat · Add the bow only when the motion is smooth</string>
